OL,3,AFrom 'dog fruit' to darling: India's
OL,4,Aavocado boom
OL,5,
OL,6,FFifteen years ago there was almost no
OL,7,Fmarket for avocados in India, remembers
OL,8,FSunil Bopaiah.
OL,10,FRipe fruit would fall off trees and be
OL,11,Featen by dogs, earning avocados the
OL,12,Funappetising name dog fruit, he says.
OL,14,FBopaiah has been working in India's
OL,15,Fplantation industry for 26 years, he's
OL,16,Fcurrently group manager at Cottanad
OL,17,FPlantations, which grows cocoa, rubber,
OL,18,Fcoffee, spices and fruits, including
OL,19,Favocado, in the hills of Wayanad in the
OL,20,Fsouthern Indian state of Kerala.
OL,23,APub: 04-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
